From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: the mouse wheel over a framed Linux program is not a click

The frame's passive grab for the click that activates it took every button,
the wheel's too: each notch activated the frame (Windows never does), and
while the grab was active the wheel's XInput 2 scrolling was the shell's.
Firefox did not scroll (David 2026-11-15). Only buttons 1-3, 8 and 9 are
grabbed now.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
@@ -718,8 +718,22 @@
     /* owner_events, and the release and motion asked for: on the frame
      * itself (its buttons, its title bar dragged) Wine must see the rest of
      * the click -- with the press alone, the close button waited for ever */
-    XGrabButton( data->display, AnyButton, AnyModifier, data->whole_window, True,
-                 ButtonPressMask | ButtonReleaseMask | PointerMotionMask, GrabModeSync, GrabModeAsync, None, None );
+    /* the buttons that click, not the wheel's (4-7): the wheel scrolls the
+     * window under the pointer without activating it, as on Windows, and the
+     * grab each notch made took the wheel's XInput 2 scrolling from the
+     * program for as long as the shell took to replay it -- Firefox did not
+     * scroll (David 2026-11-15) */
+    {
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_GRAB_WHEEL
+        static const unsigned int buttons[] = { AnyButton };
+#else
+        static const unsigned int buttons[] = { Button1, Button2, Button3, 8, 9 };
+#endif
+        unsigned int b;
+        for (b = 0; b < ARRAY_SIZE(buttons); b++)
+            XGrabButton( data->display, buttons[b], AnyModifier, data->whole_window, True,
+                         ButtonPressMask | ButtonReleaseMask | PointerMotionMask, GrabModeSync, GrabModeAsync, None, None );
+    }
 #endif
     grab_shell_keys( data->display, data->whole_window );
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_FULLSCREEN
